      <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-white/90 mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        {nearbyHikes.length} trails within 100 miles of Fresno — and they include some of the biggest names in American hiking: Half Dome, the Mist Trail, and all three of Yosemite Valley's major waterfalls
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3 text-sm">
        <div class="bg-white/10 backdrop-blur-md px-4 py-2 rounded-full border border-white/20">
          <span class="text-white/80">Closest:</span> <span class="text-white font-bold">{Math.round(closestHikes[0]?.distance)} miles</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white/10 backdrop-blur-md px-4 py-2 rounded-full border border-white/20">
          <span class="text-white/80">Drive Time:</span> <span class="text-white font-bold">{closestHikes[0]?.driveTime} min - 2 hrs</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white/10 backdrop-blur-md px-4 py-2 rounded-full border border-white/20">
          <span class="text-white/80">Difficulty:</span> <span class="text-white font-bold">Easy to Strenuous</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Scroll Indicator -->
    <div class="absolute bottom-8 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 animate-bounce">
      <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-white/50" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 14l-7 7m0 0l-7-7m7 7V3"/>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Main Content -->
  <div class="bg-stone-50 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4">

      <!-- Quick Navigation -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg p-6 mb-12 border border-stone-200">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">Jump to Section:</h2>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="#closest" class="px-4 py-2 bg-blue-50 text-blue-700 rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-100 transition-colors font-medium text-sm">
            ⚡ Closest Trails
          </a>
          <a href="#easy" class="px-4 py-2 bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-700 rounded-lg hover:bg-emerald-100 transition-colors font-medium text-sm">
            🥾 Easy Hikes
          </a>
          <a href="#moderate" class="px-4 py-2 bg-amber-50 text-amber-700 rounded-lg hover:bg-amber-100 transition-colors font-medium text-sm">
            ⛰️ Moderate Hikes
          </a>
          <a href="#strenuous" class="px-4 py-2 bg-cyan-50 text-cyan-700 rounded-lg hover:bg-cyan-100 transition-colors font-medium text-sm">
            🏔️ Strenuous Summits
          </a>
          <a href="#all" class="px-4 py-2 bg-purple-50 text-purple-700 rounded-lg hover:bg-purple-100 transition-colors font-medium text-sm">
            📍 All {nearbyHikes.length} Trails
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Intro Content -->
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-16 bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm border border-stone-200">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">Fresno Is the Closest Gate Into Yosemite's Biggest Names</h2>

        <p class="text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
          Fresno doesn't have foothills of its own worth naming, but Highway 41 runs almost due
          north out of the city and, in about {closestHikes[0]?.driveTime} minutes, drops you at
          Yosemite's South Entrance. From there, some of the most famous named trails in American
          hiking — Half Dome, the Mist Trail past Vernal and Nevada Falls, and both the upper and
          lower drops of Yosemite Falls — all sit within roughly 90 to 95 minutes of downtown
          Fresno. Tuolumne Meadows' high country (Cathedral Lakes, Clouds Rest) is real too, once
          Tioga Road opens for the season — but it's a genuinely longer trip from Fresno, covered
          honestly in the FAQ below rather than folded into the "within 2 hours" count above.
        </p>

        <p class="text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
          This site's own trail database doesn't yet reach Sequoia or Kings Canyon, so this guide
          is narrower than most of the other city pages on this site — {nearbyHikes.length} trails,
          not dozens. What it covers, though, is exactly what most "hikes near Fresno" searches are
          actually looking for. Each trail includes:
        </p>

        <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
          <li>✓ <strong>Exact distance from Fresno</strong> (measured from the trailhead, not the park boundary)</li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Trail difficulty rating</strong> (easy, moderate, strenuous)</li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Elevation gain & distance</strong></li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Parking information & fees</strong></li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Interactive trail maps</strong></li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Real-time weather conditions</strong></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Closest Hikes Section -->
      {closestHikes.length > 0 && (
        <section id="closest" class="mb-16">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-8">
            <div class="bg-blue-500 w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center text-2xl">⚡</div>
